{"abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost"},{"text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management."}]},{"text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle","type":"heading","anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every call to ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The generic ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store"},{"text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write ","type":"text"},{"code":"send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by hand — ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A fifth method, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Core-Middleware-vs-Domain-Plugins","level":2,"text":"Core Middleware vs Domain Plugins"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Core-Middleware","type":"heading","text":"Core Middleware","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" are ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"action-agnostic infrastructure","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". They never inspect the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Action"},{"type":"text","text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" needs keypaths to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"text":" properties.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" needs ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State: Equatable"},{"text":" so it can snapshot and compare.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Domain Plugins","anchor":"Domain-Plugins","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"domain-specific modules"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" that ship as separate library targets ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Importing at call sites","anchor":"Importing-at-call-sites","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because each domain plugin ships as a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"separate library target"}]},{"type":"text","text":", its state and action types are defined in that module — not in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":". A common convention is to re-export core Swidux from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@_exported import Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":", but that re-exports "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"core Swidux only"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":"; it does not re-export the plugin modules.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So any file that reads a plugin-owned slice ("},{"code":"store.analytics.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"store.paywall.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"store.killswitch.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", …) or dispatches a plugin action ("},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", …) must import that plugin’s module in "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"that","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" file:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"touches ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.analytics.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"code":"import SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"touches ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.*"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallAction"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxPaywall"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"touches only ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.ui","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":".ui(...)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (app-module types) → nothing extra","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The easy case to forget is a "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"View"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" that reads the slice for display — "},{"code":"AppState.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"AppAction.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" already import the module, but the View is a different file. Without the import you get:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["property 'isOptedOut' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxAnalytics'","property 'isPro' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxPaywall'"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is to add "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Swidux<Plugin>"},{"type":"text","text":" to that file."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Comparison","type":"heading","text":"Comparison"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Core Middleware","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Domain Plugins","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Action knowledge"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"None","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Lifecycle hooks","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":" only"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns effects"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Yes","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State coupling"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" constraint","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wiring"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Construction only"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Target","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" library"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Separate library target"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Opt-in","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Instantiate and register","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add state, action case, and register"}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"type":"heading","text":"The Decision Rule","anchor":"The-Decision-Rule","level":2},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Does the middleware need to know your action type? If ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}]},{"text":", it’s core middleware — put it in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"text":" and use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". If ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"yes","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and use ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Important","style":"important"},{"anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Hook Selection Guide"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce(state:action:)"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Capture state "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Handle domain-specific actions "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"afterReduce(state:action:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Observe state ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"flush() async","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits."}]}]}]},{"text":"Registration Order","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Registration-Order"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins use only "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so their relative order rarely matters.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"service-result action","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"KillswitchPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"verdictReceived","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"refreshSucceeded","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — fires on ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"every"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" fetch, refresh, or stream tick, not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only when the value changed, and unconditionally writes its payload to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state slice. The payload is frequently identical to what is already there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(a re-delivered entitlement, an unchanged remote config).","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Do "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" map analytics or side effects to the raw service-result action:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it fires duplicates by design. Observe the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"state slice","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — or a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"derived from it — instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State observation is already deduplicated by the framework. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"packs the observer into a value-type snapshot, lets reducers mutate the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"snapshot, then writes back via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State.apply"},{"type":"text","text":". For a leaf slice that write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a plain assignment whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" setter equality-gates "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values, so a slice whose value did not change emits no notification — and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value-diffing consumer such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsIdentity.userProperties"},{"type":"text","text":" (which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"text":" re-evaluates and diffs every non-analytics dispatch) sees exactly the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"real transitions. This dedup is a property of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", not of any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-plugin guard, so a no-op service-result cycle is silent to state","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observers without any extra reducer logic.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Next Steps","anchor":"Next-Steps"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide"},{"type":"text","text":" — Configure the built-in persistence middleware"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo middleware","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"article","metadata":{"title":"Plugin Architecture","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Explanation","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"],"anchor":"Explanation"}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","abstract":[{"text":"Coalescing persistence plugin.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"PersistencePlugin","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","abstract":[{"text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","kind":"article","title":"Undo \/ Redo"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","abstract":[{"text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","title":"Building a Domain Plugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"EntityStore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"SwiduxPlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","title":"Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"abstract":[{"text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","type":"topic","title":"Design Principles","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","title":"UndoPlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"abstract":[{"text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observation layer.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Store","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"abstract":[{"text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","title":"Architecture & Performance","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","title":"Persistence Middleware"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","title":"PluginHost"}}}